<title>PORTUGAL: Banco Comercial Portugues sees profit growth.</title>
<headline>Banco Comercial Portugues sees profit growth.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Comercial Portugues, Portugal's largest non-state bank, said that it expected the improvement in business and profitability to be sustained over 1997.</p>
<p>The bank, which posted a 21.3 percent rise in first half consolidated net profit to 13.1 billion escudos, said its confidence was based on the favourable macroeconomic outlook and growth in markets in which it was active.</p>
</text>
